# Build the real Quiz component

## Step

Promote the prototype into the component that ships. Execution is authorized
(brief Notes, Joel 2026-07-24).

Start from `73f6aaf` on `prototype/inline-quiz` —
`apps/ai-hero/src/components/mdx/quiz-prototype.tsx`,
`apps/ai-hero/src/app/quiz-prototype/page.tsx`, and the `dynamic()` registrations
in `apps/ai-hero/src/utils/compile-mdx.tsx`. Joel approved that interaction as-is,
so do not redesign the UX.

What changes from prototype to real:

- Move the component out of the `quiz-prototype` name into its permanent home and
  keep the `Quiz` / `QuizQuestion` MDX names exactly as registered — Matt is
  authoring against them.
- Validate the `data` prop with a zod schema derived from
  `QuestionResourceSchema` (`packages/survey/src/types.ts:25-52`) rather than
  trusting whatever an agent-generated MDX object literal contains. A malformed
  quiz must degrade visibly, not crash the lesson body. Note that the MDX compile
  path already has an escaping fallback for total failure
  (`compile-mdx.tsx:183-205`), which is not the same as graceful per-component
  degradation.
- Keep grading on `surveyMachine`. Keep single-answer only until
  [Decide multi-select handling](./decide-multi-select-in-the-inline-quiz.svx)
  closes.
- Handle the shuffle side effect: setting `correct` silently shuffles choices
  (`survey-machine.ts:57-60`). Decide and implement whether authors get an opt-out
  and record what you chose.
- Accessible by keyboard, labelled radios, and a visible focus state. It sits in
  a lesson body that people read on phones — the prototype was verified at 390px
  and the real one must stay that way.
- Remove `/quiz-prototype` once the real component is registered, or keep it
  deliberately as a dev fixture and say which.

**Do not build the answer endpoint here.** Wiring persistence is a separate step
that waits on [Decide what identifies an inline quiz](./decide-inline-quiz-identity.svx).
This step ships a component that grades client-side, exactly like the prototype.

## Resolved when

`<Quiz>` / `<QuizQuestion>` render from a real lesson body in the draft AI Coding
Crash Course, graded, keyboard-accessible, with invalid data degrading visibly,
and the work merged.

